From: Emir Beganovic <beganovic.emir@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: stop MHI on power down before INIT_DONE

ath12k_pci_power_up() starts MHI (setting ATH12K_MHI_POWER_ON and creating
MHI client devices such as mhi0_IPCR for qcom_mhi_qrtr) without setting
ATH12K_PCI_FLAG_INIT_DONE, which is only set later in ath12k_pci_start()
after QMI firmware initialization finishes.

If the PCI device is unbound before ath12k_pci_start() runs (for example
when board data or firmware is absent in a live environment, or when
unbinding during QMI initialization), ath12k_pci_power_down() returns
early because ATH12K_PCI_FLAG_INIT_DONE is clear. MHI is never powered
down, mhi0_IPCR and its QRTR endpoint remain registered, and
ath12k_mhi_unregister() then calls vfree(mhi_cntrl->mhi_chan). On a
subsequent rebind, QRTR routes QMI messages to the stale endpoint and
mhi_queue() faults on the unmapped mhi_chan memory.

Stop MHI in ath12k_pci_power_down() whenever ATH12K_MHI_POWER_ON is set
even if ATH12K_PCI_FLAG_INIT_DONE is still clear, mark QMI_FAIL when
ath12k_core_qmi_firmware_ready() fails, and force power off MHI when
QMI_FAIL is set so the firmware does not auto-restart during teardown.

Signed-off-by: Emir Beganovic <beganovic.emir@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c | 2 ++
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c | 3 ++-
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c | 3 +++
 3 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c
@@ -507,6 +507,8 @@ void ath12k_mhi_stop(struct ath12k_pci *ab_pci, bool is_suspend)
 	 */
 	if (is_suspend)
 		ath12k_mhi_set_state(ab_pci, ATH12K_MHI_POWER_OFF_KEEP_DEV);
+	else if (test_bit(ATH12K_FLAG_QMI_FAIL, &ab_pci->ab->dev_flags))
+		ath12k_mhi_set_state(ab_pci, ATH12K_MHI_FORCE_POWER_OFF);
 	else
 		ath12k_mhi_set_state(ab_pci, ATH12K_MHI_POWER_OFF);
 
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
@@ -1480,7 +1480,8 @@ void ath12k_pci_power_down(struct ath12k_base *ab, bool is_suspend)
 {
 	struct ath12k_pci *ab_pci = ath12k_pci_priv(ab);
 
-	if (!test_bit(ATH12K_PCI_FLAG_INIT_DONE, &ab_pci->flags))
+	if (!test_bit(ATH12K_PCI_FLAG_INIT_DONE, &ab_pci->flags) &&
+	    !test_bit(ATH12K_MHI_POWER_ON, &ab_pci->mhi_state))
 		return;
 
 	/* restore aspm in case firmware bootup fails */
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
@@ -4043,6 +4043,9 @@ static void ath12k_qmi_driver_event_work(struct work_struct *work)
 			if (!ret)
 				set_bit(ATH12K_FLAG_QMI_FW_READY_COMPLETE,
 					&ab->dev_flags);
+			else
+				set_bit(ATH12K_FLAG_QMI_FAIL,
+					&ab->dev_flags);
 
 			break;
 		case ATH12K_QMI_EVENT_HOST_CAP:
-- 
